Defects found:

1. `idempotency guard satisfied by its OWN comment/marker`  
Line 80: `if new_tok in t:`  
Exact input: `ATTR_CM_REVIEW.html` containing only `<!-- name:"ATTRibute-CM",pmid:"38197816" -->`, then run `python scripts/fix_wrong_pmids.py --apply`.  
Consequence: the script reports “already 38197816” even though the actual dashboard record was never corrected.

2. `values compared/written AS TEXT where line endings differ`  
Lines 75 and 89: text-mode read normalizes newlines, text-mode write emits platform newlines.  
Exact input: LF-only file bytes `a\nname:"ATTRibute-CM",pmid:"33725199"\nb\n`, then run `python scripts/fix_wrong_pmids.py --apply` on Windows.  
Consequence: the PMID fix also rewrites unrelated line endings to CRLF, creating false whole-file changes.

3. `status/control flag reports wrapper intent incorrectly`  
Line 88: `if args.apply:`  
Exact input: `ATTR_CM_REVIEW.html` containing `name:"ATTRibute-CM",pmid:"33725199"`, then run `python scripts/fix_wrong_pmids.py --apply --dry-run`.  
Consequence: `--apply` wins silently and modifies the file despite an explicit `--dry-run`.

Not proven from packet: check that cannot fail; probe keyed to string a fix removes; different-copy instrumentation; selector keyed to unused corpus form; merged-cell/off-by-one; zero conflated with absent; negation dropped; subprocess/wrapper status-code masking.
